title Dream blocked on a binary the overlay never shipped, and the captain's hat gets written down
prompt Keaton: Dream's first lap on the pier BLOCKED on a missing codex-code-mode-host under the nix store path -- update the nixos config for another rebuild; and seat Sound explicitly as the fleet's captain, the Fable 5 seat that fixes other ship and pier issues.
think Dream's refusal was the discipline working end to end: three bounded casts, BLOCKED named as a machine limit rather than a tree defect, zero files moved, no state inferred. The fault is real and simple -- codex 0.150 grew a second executable, and the feature that spawns it (code_mode_host) reads stable-and-default-true in `codex features list`, verified against the local 0.150 CLI, so the tool router demands $out/bin/codex-code-mode-host on every tool call and the nix overlay installed only codex itself.
think Two fixes at two speeds. NOW: every codex exec line in the Dream launcher carries --disable code_mode_host -- the same --disable flag Mind's finite-retry fix uses -- so the classic tool path serves before any rebuild, with the why printed once on the card. PROPER: the overlay gains a second pinned fetchurl, codeModeHost, the artifact upstream ships under the same release tag, fetched here and hashed -- sha256 b476...4fc5, 21,208,013 bytes -- untarred and installed beside codex in the same installPhase, self-checking the same way.
think Keaton also cp -r'd the pier tree to ~/grain-dream -- the grain-mind pattern arriving at the second jailed star, so no jailed loop shares a checkout with Hush's. The charter's Dream host cell records the clone.
obs The captain's hat is now written where the fleet reads: the charter's Sound row and the Sound seat card both carry it. As the one interactive Fable 5 seat, Sound repairs any ship or pier whose own hand is stopped -- reading a stopped peer's clone is welcome, editing it is not (fix the shared tree and let its round-open pull carry the cure), a cross-lane repair on Keaton's word is captaincy rather than trespass, and it ends where the stopped hand can run again. That sentence is a description of this whole week made law.
obs The rebuild line for Keaton's outer terminal is unchanged from the card: bash /home/keeper/grain/nixos/rebuild-outer.sh -- and until it runs, Dream's loop line already works through the disable flag, so the pier does not wait on the rebuild.
loom binary_missing=codex-code-mode-host feature=code_mode_host default=true artifact_bytes=21208013 exec_lines_flagged=3 fixes=2_speeds clones_now=2
